---
name: windows-ui-testing-without-a-desktop
description: How to drive real JusPrin UI gestures on the Windows box when the RDP session is disconnected (SetCursorPos and screen capture both die; send WM_ messages and read geometry instead)
metadata: 
  node_type: memory
  type: project
  originSessionId: c818cfcf-07b0-4d84-a4d6-a69c1bd9fdde
  modified: 2026-10-21T21:53:29.293Z
---

When the RDP session to the Windows verification box is **disconnected** (`query session` shows state `Disc` for the `guitest` session), `SetCursorPos`/`mouse_event` silently do nothing — `GetCursorPos` keeps returning 0,0 — and `Graphics.CopyFromScreen` throws "The handle is invalid". Only a *connected* session has an input desktop.

**Why:** This looks exactly like an application bug — gestures appear to have no effect and screenshots fail — so it can burn a long time before you realise the session, not the code, is the problem.

**How to apply:**
- Check `query session` first when input or capture stops working.
- Real UI testing still works without a desktop: `SendMessageTimeout` WM_LBUTTONDOWN / WM_MOUSEMOVE / WM_LBUTTONUP / WM_LBUTTONDBLCLK straight to the child HWND. This goes through the real wxMSW window procedure, real `SetCapture`, and real double-click handling — strictly more real than the harness's `ProcessEvent` injection, which bypasses `MSWWindowProc` entirely.
- A faithful drag must hold the pointer at a fixed **screen** x and recompute the client x from the target window's live `GetWindowRect` each step. Holding client x fixed makes a moving splitter run away, because the app converts with `ClientToScreen` against the window's current position.
- Screenshots still work disconnected through `PrintWindow(hwnd, hdc, 2)` (PW_RENDERFULLCONTENT): it draws the GL canvas and WebView2 panes (confirmed 2026-10-21). CopyFromScreen may not throw but returns a blank white image. Mid-redraw, the canvas and settings panel come out grey, so capture once the app is idle.
- Read results from `EnumChildWindows` + `GetWindowRect` rather than pixels; assert that sibling columns tile the client rect exactly, which catches overlaps a per-window size check cannot see.
- P/Invoke `GetWindowTextW` must be declared `CharSet=CharSet.Unicode`, or the StringBuilder is marshalled as ANSI and the W call overruns the buffer and crashes PowerShell.
- The harness holds `shell_integration_harness.exe` open; kill it before relinking or the link fails with LNK1104.
- See [[windows-build-machine]] for the Mesa/GL and toolchain facts.
// Scratch DevTools driver for the WebView2 pages.
//   node cdp.mjs list
//   node cdp.mjs eval <urlSubstring> <js>
//   node cdp.mjs shot <urlSubstring> <out.png>
import { writeFileSync } from 'node:fs';

const [, , command, match, arg] = process.argv;
const targets = await (await fetch('http://127.0.0.1:9222/json/list')).json();
if (command === 'list') {
  for (const t of targets) console.log(t.type, t.url.slice(0, 120), t.title);
  process.exit(0);
}
const pages = targets.filter((t) => t.type === 'page' && t.url.includes(match));
if (pages.length === 0) {
  console.error('no page matches', match);
  process.exit(2);
}
const socket = new WebSocket(pages[0].webSocketDebuggerUrl);
await new Promise((resolve) => socket.addEventListener('open', resolve));
let next = 0;
const call = (method, params = {}) =>
  new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
    const id = ++next;
    const listener = (event) => {
      const message = JSON.parse(event.data);
      if (message.id !== id) return;
      socket.removeEventListener('message', listener);
      message.error ? reject(new Error(JSON.stringify(message.error))) : resolve(message.result);
    };
    socket.addEventListener('message', listener);
    socket.send(JSON.stringify({ id, method, params }));
  });
if (command === 'eval') {
  const result = await call('Runtime.evaluate', { expression: arg, awaitPromise: true, returnByValue: true });
  console.log(JSON.stringify(result.result.value ?? result.exceptionDetails ?? result.result, null, 1));
} else if (command === 'type') {
  // Focus the composer, type as a keyboard does, then Enter.
  await call('Runtime.evaluate', { expression: "document.querySelector('textarea').focus()" });
  await call('Input.insertText', { text: arg });
  for (const type of ['keyDown', 'keyUp'])
    await call('Input.dispatchKeyEvent', { type, key: 'Enter', code: 'Enter', windowsVirtualKeyCode: 13, text: type === 'keyDown' ? '\r' : undefined });
  console.log('typed', arg);
} else if (command === 'shot') {
  const result = await call('Page.captureScreenshot', { format: 'png' });
  writeFileSync(arg, Buffer.from(result.data, 'base64'));
  console.log('wrote', arg);
}
socket.close();
process.exit(0);

